_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2016-05-31T10:21:02Z","label":{"name":"bug-vim","color":"fc2929"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/222651512","html_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/4848#issuecomment-222651512","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/4848","id":222651512,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMjY1MTUxMg==","user":{"login":"ZyX-I","id":322097,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjA5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/322097?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I","html_url":"https://github.com/ZyX-I","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-05-31T10:32:02Z","updated_at":"2016-05-31T10:32:02Z","body":"Vim has exactly the same behaviour:\n\n```\n% vim -u NONE -i /tmp/viminfo -N --cmd 'call histadd(\":\", \"test\")' --cmd cq\n% vim -u NONE -i /tmp/viminfo -N --cmd 'call histdel(\":\", \"test\")' --cmd cq\n% cat /tmp/viminfo | grep '^:test'\n:test\n```\n\nProblem is that there is no way to know whether `test` entry is the deleted one or the new one coming from another session (and deleted entries are not actually kept).\n\nThe only way to fix this is to keep deleted history entries list, but this again is not going to help if you have more then one Neovim instance running: other Neovim instances will simply write that history line again if they were run before histdel and exit after. And I do not like the idea of keeping deleted entries in the file marked as deleted. Note that e.g. shells have _no_ way to delete history entries at all, except for “kill all shells, edit the file” which works with Neovim as well (need to edit with `-i NONE` if done by Neovim).\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/222651512/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ZyX-I","id":322097,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjA5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/322097?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I","html_url":"https://github.com/ZyX-I","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZyX-I/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":676813266,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50Njc2ODEzMjY2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/events/676813266","actor":{"log